---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const players = (await getCollection('nba')).sort((a, b) => a.data.rank - b.data.rank);

const POSITIONS = ['PG', 'SG', 'SF', 'PF', 'C'] as const;
const POSITION_LABEL: Record<(typeof POSITIONS)[number], string> = {
  PG: 'Point Guard',
  SG: 'Shooting Guard',
  SF: 'Small Forward',
  PF: 'Power Forward',
  C: 'Center',
};

// Depth chart: everyone grouped by position, in rank order — PG1 is my
// highest-ranked point guard, PG2 the next, and so on. This is "phase one" of
// the guide below: settle each position before touching the overall list.
const byPosition = Object.fromEntries(
  POSITIONS.map((pos) => [pos, players.filter((p) => p.data.position === pos)]),
) as Record<(typeof POSITIONS)[number], typeof players>;

const cards = players.map((entry) => {
  const pos = entry.data.position;
  const depthIndex = byPosition[pos].findIndex((p) => p.id === entry.id) + 1;
  const posColumn = POSITIONS.indexOf(pos) + 1;
  return {
    entry,
    depthLabel: `${pos}${depthIndex}`,
    style:
      `--grouped-col:${posColumn};--grouped-row:${depthIndex};` +
      `--ranked-row:${entry.data.rank};view-transition-name:player-${entry.id};`,
  };
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Building the NBA top 25"
  description="How the position depth chart and era duels turn into one ranked list — with a live demo."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-16">
    <a
      href="/fun/nba"
      class="text-sm text-text-muted underline decoration-border underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-accent hover:decoration-accent"
    >
      ← Back to the top 25
    </a>

    <p class="mt-6 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Off the clock</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      How the top 25 actually gets built
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-text-muted">
      Ranking 25 players across seven decades directly is hopeless — you end up comparing a 1960s
      center to a 2020s point guard with nothing in common. Two phases make it tractable instead.
    </p>

    <ol class="mt-8 max-w-2xl list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-text-muted">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-text">Position battles.</strong> Build a depth chart — every point guard
        stacked against every other point guard, same for each position. Comparable skill sets,
        comparable roles.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-text">Era duels.</strong> Where two or three players overlapped and both
        have a real case for "best in the league right now," settle it head-to-head before merging
        everyone into one list.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="mt-14 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Phase 1: the depth chart</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-text-muted">
      Same 25 players as the top 25, just sorted into position groups first. Hit the button to watch
      them merge back into the actual ranking.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-6 flex justify-center">
      <button
        type="button"
        id="roster-toggle"
        class="rounded border border-accent bg-accent/10 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-accent transition-colors hover:bg-accent/20"
      >
        Merge into final ranking
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="roster-scroll mt-8 overflow-x-auto">
      <div class="roster-wrap grouped">
        <div class="grouped-headers">
          {POSITIONS.map((pos) => <div class="grouped-header">{POSITION_LABEL[pos]}</div>)}
        </div>
        <ul class="roster">
          {
            cards.map(({ entry, depthLabel, style }) => (
              <li class="roster-card" style={style}>
                <span class="roster-depth">{depthLabel}</span>
                <span class="roster-rank">#{entry.data.rank}</span>
                <span class="roster-name">{entry.data.name}</span>
                <span class="roster-era">{entry.data.era}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-center text-xs text-text-muted">
      Runs on the View Transitions API — same static HTML/CSS/JS GitHub Pages already serves, no
      server needed. Falls back to an instant snap if a browser (or reduced-motion setting) doesn't
      support it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Phase 2: era duels</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-text-muted">
      The depth chart still leaves ties — players who overlapped and both have a real claim to "best
      in the league" in a given stretch. Two of those calls, straight from the reasoning already
      behind the rankings above:
    </p>

    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-text-muted">1980s · SF/PG</p>
        <h3 class="mt-1 font-display text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">Bird vs. Magic</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          Bird gets the nod (#7 vs. #8) — better defender, ahead-of-his-time shooter, and did it with
          lesser teams around him. Magic's case is the best-passer-ever argument and a Swiss-army-knife
          game; he just never had to do it without Kareem and Worthy next to him.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-text-muted">2000s · C/PF/SG</p>
        <h3 class="mt-1 font-display text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">Shaq vs. Duncan vs. Kobe</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          Landed #4, #5, #6 — in that order, back-to-back. Shaq's peak was the most dominant of the
          three, which is exactly why neither Duncan nor Kobe was ever really considered the best
          player in the league in a given year despite both being inner-circle greats. Duncan edges
          Kobe on longevity and two-way impact; Kobe's efficiency and playing Robin to Shaq's Batman
          cost him the last half-step.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-text-muted">
      Do that for every position and every overlapping era, merge the results by rank, and you get
      the <a href="/fun/nba" class="underline decoration-border underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent hover:decoration-accent">top 25</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .grouped-headers {
    display: none;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(9rem, 1fr));
    gap: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .roster-wrap.grouped .grouped-headers {
    display: grid;
  }
  .grouped-header {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .roster {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    max-width: 32rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .roster-wrap.grouped .roster {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(9rem, 1fr));
    max-width: none;
    margin-inline: 0;
    gap: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
  }

  .roster-card {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: var(--ranked-row);
    display: flex;
    min-width: 0;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background-color: var(--surface);
    padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
  }
  .roster-wrap.grouped .roster-card {
    grid-column: var(--grouped-col);
    grid-row: var(--grouped-row);
  }

  .roster-depth {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .roster-rank {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .roster-name {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .roster-era {
    margin-left: auto;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .roster-wrap.grouped .roster-era {
    display: none;
  }

  ::view-transition-group(*) {
    animation-duration: var(--duration-slow);
    animation-timing-function: var(--ease-out);
  }
</style>

<script>
  function bindRosterToggle() {
    const wrap = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.roster-wrap');
    const button = document.getElementById('roster-toggle');
    if (!wrap || !button || button.dataset.bound === 'true') return;
    button.dataset.bound = 'true';

    let grouped = true;
    const setLabel = () => {
      button.textContent = grouped ? 'Merge into final ranking' : 'Split into position groups';
    };
    setLabel();

    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      grouped = !grouped;
      const apply = () => {
        wrap.classList.toggle('grouped', grouped);
        setLabel();
      };

      const reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      if (!reducedMotion && document.startViewTransition) {
        document.startViewTransition(apply);
      } else {
        apply();
      }
    });
  }

  bindRosterToggle();
  document.addEventListener('astro:after-swap', bindRosterToggle);
</script>
